 # Keep the session in the working repository
+
+Before invoking `/cd` or asking the user to enter it, resolve background command handles opened by
+this task and its subagents. Wait for useful work to finish; terminate only verified obsolete commands
+owned by this task. Consume their completion and release their handles. A completed subagent must
+resolve its outstanding commands before handing work back. When the native host terminal list is
+accessible, confirm it has no active terminals before requesting the directory change. Never send the
+user to `/cd` with known active task-owned terminals.
+
+An unknown command handle or an empty OS process scan does not prove the native terminal list is empty;
+a directory guard error alone does not prove a live process remains. If native controls are unavailable
+or the guard fails, explain the exact gap. Use the host's supported `/ps` to inspect the current session
+and `/stop` only when its remaining commands are verified obsolete and task-owned; when agent access
+is unavailable, give the user that native recovery step before retrying `/cd`. Do not claim cleanup
+without completion evidence, restart the host, or stop another session's commands.
 
 When the task moves to a different repository or worktree, invoke the host's native
 `/cd <absolute-path>` command immediately after the target directory exists and before continuing
